ntry><doc-number>8138233</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </patcit><patcit ucid="JP-9040680-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>9040680</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id> <sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </patcit> <patcit ucid="JP-9176323-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>9176323</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="US-5210248-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>US</country><doc-number>5210248</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="US-5284707-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>US</country><doc-number>5284707</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="US-5605958-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>US</country><doc-number>5605958</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1055718A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KONDO SATOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKA KOICHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TORAY INDUSTRIES</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KONDOU, SATOSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKA, KOICHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TORAY INDUSTRIES, INC.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KONDOU SATOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKA KOICHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KONDOU, SATOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKA, KOICHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An optical article which has an organic silicon compound layer on the surface thereof, characterized as exhibiting a contact angle for an artificial finger print liquid on said surface of 60 DEG  or more and a falling angle for the artificial finger print liquid of 30 DEG  or less; a method for coating an optical article with an organic silicon compound which involves vaporizing the compound in a vacuum vessel, characterized in that the organic silicon compound has been subjected to condensation polymerization in advance: and a specific organic silicon compound for use in the optical article. The optical article has advantages in that it is less susceptible to staining and is easy to remove stains. The optical article can be suitably used in applications such as image planes of various displays, plains for display in various display devices, optical filters, eyeglass lenses, optical lenses, luminaries, cases or show windows for exhibition, frames for picture, windowpanes and the like; and also for optical goods attached to the items described above.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un article optique recouvert par une couche d'un composé organo-silicié, qui possède, pour un liquide d'étalonnage artificiel, un angle de contact avec la surface de 60 DEG  ou davantage et un angle de chute de 30 DEG  ou moins; un procédé permettant de recouvrir un article optique avec un composé organo-silicié, qui consiste à vaporiser ledit composé dans une enceinte à vide après l'avoir soumis à une polycondensation; et un composé organo-silicié spécifique destiné à être utilisé avec ledit article optique. L'article optique présente comme avantage le fait qu'il se tache moins et que les taches sont faciles à enlever. Il peut être utilisé dans des applications telles que plans image d'afficheurs, lisses de dispositifs d'affichage, filtres optiques, verres de lunettes, lentilles ophtalmiques, luminaires, vitrines d'exposition ou étalages, cadres de tableaux, panneaux vitrés, etc., ainsi que pour des articles optiques associés aux items ci-dessus.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>